n disease genes are determined by the direction of replication in E. coli</article-title><source>Nat. Genet.</source><year>1995</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7663518</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sarkar</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Boudi</surname><given-names>FB</given-names></name><name><surname>Reddy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CTG repeats show bimodal amplification in E. coli</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1998</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>531</fpage><lpage>540</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9827805</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cai</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pytlos</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinden</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Generation of long tracts of disease-associated DNA repeats</article-title><source>BioTechniques</source><year>2005</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>247</fpage><lpage>253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15727131</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fire</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>SQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rolling replication of short DNA circles</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>1995</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>4641</fpage><lpage>4645</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7753856</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blanco</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernad</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lazaro</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Garmendia</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Salas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Highly efficient DNA synthesis by the phage phi 29 DNA polymerase. Symmetrical mode of DNA replication</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>1989</year><volume>264</volume><fpage>8935</fpage><lpage>8940</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2498321</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hutchison</surname><given-names>CA</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>HO</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfannkoch</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Venter</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cell-free cloning using phi29 DNA polymerase</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>17332</fpage><lpage>17336</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16286637</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lizardi</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Bray-Ward</surn